h about $200.6M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 49% in the 2020 crash, 31% in the 2022 bear market and 70% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 62% below its DCF fair value of $504, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 50%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $338 to $767 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Technology peers: P/E 13.6 vs 26.7, EV/EBITDA 10.0 vs 16.4 and P/FCF 10.2 vs 25.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 45% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 9.8% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 13 covering analysts target $199 on average, 5% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 45% clears the cost of capital of 8.5% by 36pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.57).","It runs a 61% gross margin and converts 18% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.77x.","ROE of 228% is amplified by 25.3x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 2.4% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.0x net debt to EBITDA ($1.7B of cash against $3.0B of debt), with interest covered 8.2x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.3, in the safe zone).","The current ratio of 1.00 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.9% over 3 years, 9.6% over 5 years and 11.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.5% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00 and a backlog worth 99% of annual revenue.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 25, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.7%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $1.4M sold).","It returns 16.6% a year to shareholders (16.6% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 5.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 14.6% of the float, 7.1 days to cover."],"people":["With about 19,460 employees, each generates about $334K of revenue, in line with the Technology median, and productivity has risen 11.4% a year.","That works out to $60K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (8x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":93,"head":"Invest: trades 62% below fair value of $504; ROIC 44.6% vs WACC 8.5%.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 59, gates 15/25)","Trades 62% below fair value of $504","ROIC 44.6% vs WACC 8.5%","FCF margin 18.1%","Revenue grew 9.6%/yr over 5y"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":428.18,"vc":{"base":503.74,"base_src":"dcf","bear":338.42,"bull":766.88,"alt_median":210.88,"n_alt":1,"gap":1.9933,"dispersion":0.4992,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (50% dispersion)","DCF is 199% above the other models' median ($211)"]},"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"IT","date":"2026-11-06"}